  "necessity_paragraph": "The patient presents with recurrent episodes of dizziness and presyncope in the setting of known sick sinus syndrome and atherosclerotic heart disease (G45.9, I25.10, I49.5). Given the recent transient cerebral ischemic attack, continuous mobile cardiac telemetry (CPT 93229) is ordered to evaluate for potential arrhythmic causes of cerebral hypoperfusion and to optimize rate control. The payer denied the claim under Reason Code CO-197, indicating that the required precertification or authorization was not obtained prior to the service date; however, the clinical indication demonstrates that this diagnostic procedure is medically necessary to address the patient's documented symptoms and underlying cardiac conditions."
